-- Explicit `Basics.eq` does not accept a type variable just because it
-- sits inside a structure: the rigid `a` inside `[ x ]` has no `eq`, so
-- `same` is `missing_where_constraint` in its body; the flex `x` inside
-- `( x, 1 )` gets the requirement, so `same2` is inferred `where a.eq` and
-- its call with two functions is `not_equatable` — never a clean check
-- whose built program compares two functions at run time and prints
-- `different` twice. Since 2026-10-02 `Basics.eq` asks for `eq` through a
-- `where` clause, as `==` does (static-dispatch-spike.md §3.1, amended);
-- it was the `equatable` marker's walk (checker-v2.md §11.4) before.

same : a, a → Bool
same x y = Basics.eq [ x ] [ y ]


same2 x y = Basics.eq ( x, 1 ) ( y, 1 )


use : Bool
use = same2 (λn → n + 1) λn → n + 1
